WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.294 --> 00:00:07.451
The warship continued to fire at us. Cannonballs fell into the sea around us, but none of them touched the Nautilus

2
00:00:07.452 --> 00:00:14.626
. If any of them hit the submarine, we would be in serious trouble, yet Captain Nemo did not appear on the

3
00:00:14.627 --> 00:00:19.967
platform. "Professor, we must do everything we can to get out of this situation," said

4
00:00:19.968 --> 00:00:22.110
Ned. Conseil nodded in

5
00:00:22.111 --> 00:00:29.610
agreement. "Let's try to signal the warship," said Ned. "Perhaps then they'll understand that we're good people, not connected to Captain

6
00:00:29.611 --> 00:00:32.547
Nemo." Ned pulled out his handkerchief to wave in the

7
00:00:32.548 --> 00:00:37.181
air. But he had scarcely revealed it when he was struck by a fist and fell to the deck.

8
00:00:37.182 --> 00:00:43.681
"Fool! What do you think you're doing?" bellowed Captain Nemo, whose arrival had gone unnoticed.

9
00:00:43.682 --> 00:00:49.840
The captain's face was purple with rage as he roared at Ned and shook the harpooner by the shoulders.

10
00:00:49.841 --> 00:00:57.419
Then he abandoned Ned and turned to face the warship, which was still raining cannonballs onto the sea around the Nautilus

11
00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:04.244
. "So, ship of a cursed nation, you know who I am!" said Captain Nemo in a powerful

12
00:01:04.245 --> 00:01:09.585
voice. "I don't need to see your flag to know who you are, but I'll show you

13
00:01:09.586 --> 00:01:14.911
mine!" The captain held up a black flag similar to the one he had placed at the South

14
00:01:14.912 --> 00:01:23.149
Pole. At that moment a cannonball struck the Nautilus without damaging it and bounced into the sea. The captain seemed

15
00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:28.038
unfazed. "Go below!" he said to me. "You and your companions, go below

16
00:01:28.039 --> 00:01:32.220
now!" "Captain, are you going to attack that vessel?" I

17
00:01:32.221 --> 00:01:35.720
asked. "Professor, I'm going to sink

18
00:01:35.721 --> 00:01:38.641
it." "You wouldn't do that!" I said in

19
00:01:38.642 --> 00:01:48.704
horror. "I will," he said coldly, "and I advise you not to judge me. Fate has shown you what you ought not to have seen. The attack has begun."

20
00:01:48.705 --> 00:01:53.292
"What is this vessel that attacks us? What country does it represent?"

21
00:01:53.293 --> 00:01:58.347
"It's better if you don't know. I say to you once more: Go below."

22
00:01:58.348 --> 00:02:06.942
There was nothing for us to do but obey. About fifteen crew members surrounded the captain, all looking with hatred at the approaching vessel.

23
00:02:06.943 --> 00:02:11.037
The same desire for vengeance seemed to fill every soul.

24
00:02:11.038 --> 00:02:18.960
I was leaving the platform at the moment another projectile struck the Nautilus , and I heard the captain shouting, "Strike, mad

25
00:02:18.961 --> 00:02:21.803
vessel! Shower us with your useless

26
00:02:21.804 --> 00:02:26.343
cannonballs. You'll never escape the battering ram of the Nautilus , but you won't

27
00:02:26.344 --> 00:02:31.014
perish here. I won't have your wreckage mingling with that of the

28
00:02:31.015 --> 00:02:35.760
sacred Avenger !" I returned to the gallery, where I could see by the instruments that we

29
00:02:35.761 --> 00:02:39.673
were speeding up. The Nautilus was soon beyond range of

30
00:02:39.674 --> 00:02:43.236
the warship's guns. Around four in the afternoon, I returned

31
00:02:43.237 --> 00:02:47.990
to the platform. The captain was pacing while looking at the ship, now five or

32
00:02:47.991 --> 00:02:51.903
six miles away. He allowed it to pursue us, but he

33
00:02:51.904 --> 00:02:57.490
did not attack. Perhaps if I said something, I could put a stop to this terrible episode before

34
00:02:57.491 --> 00:02:59.498
it began. "Captain—"

35
00:02:59.499 --> 00:03:09.818
I said. "Silence!" he roared. "I am the law and I am the judge! I am the oppressed and on that ship is

36
00:03:09.819 --> 00:03:19.421
the oppressor! Thanks to him, I have lost all that I loved, cherished, and respected—country, wife, children, father,

37
00:03:19.422 --> 00:03:29.048
and mother. I saw all of them perish! All that I hate is there! I have nothing to discuss with you,

38
00:03:29.049 --> 00:03:36.627
Professor Aronnax." I cast a last look at the warship, which was steaming toward us, and joined Ned and Conseil in

39
00:03:36.628 --> 00:03:43.879
the gallery. "We must flee this submarine!" I exclaimed. "I don't know where that warship is from, but it will be sunk

40
00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:50.374
before night. In any case, it's better for us to perish with it than to be part of a revenge that we don't

41
00:03:50.375 --> 00:03:58.445
fully understand." "I agree," said Ned. "The moon should be almost full tonight. We can escape when the ship is near enough to hear us or

42
00:03:58.446 --> 00:04:02.024
see us." Night arrived and the Nautilus remained on

43
00:04:02.025 --> 00:04:06.191
the surface. Several times I thought the submarine was preparing

44
00:04:06.192 --> 00:04:11.842
to attack. But instead Captain Nemo continued to allow his enemy to approach before darting ahead

45
00:04:11.843 --> 00:04:15.754
of it. The three of us waited for our opportunity to take

46
00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:24.167
action. We hardly spoke at all because we were too nervous. Several times Ned wanted to throw himself into the water, but I forced him to

47
00:04:24.168 --> 00:04:29.493
wait. At three o'clock in the morning, full of uneasiness, I mounted the

48
00:04:29.494 --> 00:04:34.009
platform. Captain Nemo was standing near his flag, which was blowing in the

49
00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:43.168
wind. His eyes never left the warship. The intensity of his look seemed to draw it toward us more surely than if we had been towing

50
00:04:43.169 --> 00:04:47.310
it. The moon was overhead, and Jupiter was rising in the

51
00:04:47.311 --> 00:04:54.056
east. The sky and the sea rivaled each other in tranquility while passions boiled aboard the

52
00:04:54.057 --> 00:04:59.239
Nautilus . I remained on the platform until six o'clock without Captain Nemo speaking

53
00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:05.723
to me. The warship lay about a mile and a half from us, and it began firing again with the first light

54
00:05:05.724 --> 00:05:12.556
of day. The moment was approaching when the Nautilus would attack its enemy, and my companions and I would leave Captain

55
00:05:12.557 --> 00:05:19.723
Nemo forever. The lieutenant came up on the platform, accompanied by several crewmen, who began to prepare

56
00:05:19.724 --> 00:05:27.715
for battle. The railing around the platform was removed; the pilothouse and electric light were lowered until they were level with the surface of the

57
00:05:27.716 --> 00:05:30.419
submarine. I returned to my companions in the

58
00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:36.429
gallery. The Nautilus was slowing down, and I knew that Captain Nemo was allowing the warship to draw

59
00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:40.286
near. Now I could hear the sound of cannon fire more

60
00:05:40.287 --> 00:05:44.763
distinctly. "My friends, the hour for battle has arrived," I

61
00:05:44.764 --> 00:05:51.493
announced. Ned was determined, Conseil calm, myself so nervous that I didn't know what to

62
00:05:51.494 --> 00:06:00.256
do. We went into the library; from here all we had to do was pass through a door, climb the stairs to the platform, and make our

63
00:06:00.257 --> 00:06:04.755
escape. But the moment I opened the door, I heard the hatch above us slam

64
00:06:04.756 --> 00:06:07.922
shut. As Ned rushed onto the stairs, I stopped

65
00:06:07.923 --> 00:06:13.906
him. A familiar hissing told me that the reservoirs were filling and the submarine was

66
00:06:13.907 --> 00:06:16.390
descending. I understood the

67
00:06:16.391 --> 00:06:24.073
maneuver. Captain Nemo wanted to strike the warship from underwater, where the bottom of the ship lacked protective plating and was most

68
00:06:24.074 --> 00:06:28.168
vulnerable. We scarcely had time to think, but took refuge in my

69
00:06:28.169 --> 00:06:33.993
cabin. I waited and listened intently; all my senses concentrated in my

70
00:06:33.994 --> 00:06:40.049
hearing. The Nautilus accelerated, and I knew it was preparing to attack the ship with the battering ram on its bow.

71
00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:44.906
The whole submarine trembled as it hit the warship. I screamed!

72
00:06:44.907 --> 00:06:53.319
Unable to stand it any longer, I ran to the gallery. Captain Nemo was standing before one of the windows, watching the warship sink.

73
00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:58.978
I could not bear to look. When it was all over, he returned to his cabin.

74
00:06:58.979 --> 00:07:05.801
Through the open door, I saw a portrait of a young woman, undoubtedly his wife, and his two children.

75
00:07:05.802 --> 00:07:14.000
Captain Nemo gazed at them, stretched out his arms, and kneeling down, burst into sobs.

